%% Phase 1 of the sandbox-local bootstrap: everything up.nu does before Flux takes over.
%% This is the code in infra/ (up.nu, plan.nu, render.nu, deploy-repo.nu, flux.nu), run end to end on 2026-10-19.
%% A target that does not set gitops: true skips steps 8 to 11 and applies its layers itself.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Op as Operator
    participant Up as infra/up.nu
    participant Img as infra/images.nu
    participant Reg as registry :5000<br/>(container polar-registry)
    participant Ren as infra/render.nu
    participant Pods as agent-pods.nu<br/>(scratch namespace)
    participant Cat as the renderers<br/>(render cache)
    participant Adm as polar-admin-grant<br/>(infra/tools.nu)
    participant Sec as targets/T/secrets.nu
    participant Dep as deploy-repo.nu
    participant DGit as deployment git server<br/>(container on the host)
    participant Fx as flux.nu
    participant K as Kubernetes API

    Op->>Up: nu infra/up.nu sandbox-local --user U --email E
    Up->>Up: read targets/T/target.nu (charts, layers, waits, gitops: true)<br/>build_plan (plan.nu) prints the steps and why any is skipped

    Note over Up,K: 1 preflight
    Up->>K: kubectl get nodes, a container runtime exists when a step needs one
    Up->>Up: the SOPS files decrypt (or the secrets already exist)

    Note over Up,Reg: 2 agent images (only with --dev, else the registry must already hold them)
    Up->>Img: images sync (the agents the render will ask)
    Img->>Reg: nix build, skopeo copy to the registry (nu infra/images.nu import fills it from a published account instead)

    Note over Up,K: 3 render
    Up->>K: discard cluster-inputs.nuon if it was made for another cluster (CA fingerprint)
    Up->>Pods: resolve.nu collect-scaffolds: for each agent image whose scaffold is not cached<br/>under its digest, run IMAGE --scaffold as a pod (pulled Always), then delete the namespace
    Pods-->>Up: one scaffold per agent, in a temporary directory (POLAR_SCAFFOLD_DIR)
    Up->>Ren: nu infra/render.nu T
    Ren->>Ren: resolve the registry once (registry.nu: POLAR_NODE_REGISTRY, the target, cluster.nuon)<br/>and export it, the charts' Dhall reads it
    Ren->>Cat: each chart's main.nu (dhall-render.nu: dhall-to-yaml through the chart cache),<br/>then render-catalog.nu and resolve.nu per workload (through the catalog cache)
    Cat-->>Ren: manifests/NAME.yaml and NAME-resources.yaml
    Ren->>Ren: pin every image by digest from the image lock (a pinning target)<br/>checks: apply order, service accounts, Job replacement, image pull policies,<br/>cert-issuer identity, CA provisioning, layers
    Ren-->>Up: manifests/ (52 files for sandbox-local), identical on every run

    Note over Up,Reg: 4 images (only with --dev): what the rendered manifests reference
    Up->>Img: images needed (reads image: from manifests/), then sync as in step 2

    Note over Up,K: 5 namespaces (before any secret can be made)
    Up->>K: kubectl apply manifests/namespaces.yaml

    Note over Up,K: 6 cluster CA
    Up->>Adm: polar-admin-grant bootstrap-ca (skipped if Secret cert-issuer-ca exists)
    Adm->>K: straight to the API with your kubeconfig, there is no broker yet:<br/>Secret cert-issuer-ca (key and certificate), ConfigMap polar-ca (certificate)<br/>created once and never overwritten

    Note over Up,K: 7 secrets (which Flux does not own and never prunes)
    Up->>Sec: secrets.nu TARGET_DIR REPO_ROOT
    Sec->>Sec: sops decrypt secrets.sops.yaml and user.sops.yaml (rage, your SSH key)
    Sec->>K: upsert neo4j-secret, polar-graph-pw, cassini-shutdown-token, jira-secret,<br/>oci-registry-auth, keycloak-admin-secret, keycloak-db-secret

    Note over Up,DGit: 8 the deployment git server
    Up->>Dep: deploy-repo.nu ensure T
    Dep->>Dep: first time only: ~/.config/polar-deploy/T/ gets a CA, a server certificate<br/>(the cluster-local name Flux will use, and localhost), and client certificates for<br/>"pipeline" (writes) and "flux" (reads), made with openssl. Not Polar's CA.
    Dep->>DGit: run the polar-git-server image by digest with --restart=always, --tmpfs /tmp,<br/>repository deploy-T, writers [pipeline], readers [flux]
    Dep->>DGit: check it answers over mTLS as "pipeline"

    Note over Up,DGit: 9 publish
    Up->>Dep: deploy-repo.nu publish T
    Dep->>Dep: refuse a target that is not rendered, an image not pinned by digest,<br/>a dirty tree (unless --allow-dirty)
    Dep->>Dep: build the tree: layers/ (every layer but flux, with a config-hash fingerprint<br/>in the pod template of each workload that reads a ConfigMap), flux/ (GitRepository and<br/>a Kustomization per layer), provenance.json, a README
    Dep->>Dep: sign with git x509 (gpgsm, a GnuPG home beside the PKI, no prompt), verify the commit
    Dep->>DGit: push over mTLS as "pipeline", ACL by certificate identity, push-log.jsonl
    Dep-->>Up: the deployment repo at COMMIT (nothing committed if the render is unchanged)

    Note over Up,K: 10 install Flux
    Up->>Fx: flux.nu install T
    Fx->>DGit: clone as "flux" and git verify-commit against the deployment CA,<br/>a head that is not signed stops everything here, before the cluster is touched
    Fx->>K: apply the Flux controllers, wait for the CRDs and Deployments
    Fx->>K: Service polar-deploy-git and an EndpointSlice to the host,<br/>Secret deploy-repo-auth (the "flux" certificate, key and the deployment CA)
    Fx->>K: apply the GitRepository and wait until it has fetched the repository
    Fx->>K: apply the Kustomizations (from the verified clone)
    Fx-->>Up: Flux is running and has the repository

    Note over Up,K: 11 wait for Flux: phase2-flux.png
    Up->>Fx: flux.nu wait T
